  "raw": {
    "https://www.msujobs.msstate.edu/": {
      "title": "Home",
      "description": "Home | MSU Jobs Skip to main content Skip to main menu Search MSSTATE Toggle mobile search field Search myState on Mississippi State University Toggle mobile search field Menu Home Careers Benefits & Perks Work/Life Balance About Starkville Applicant Notices Campus Security MSState Calendars A-Z Index Directory Maps Newsroom Contact myState on Mississippi State University Directory on Mississippi State University News Contact Search MSSTATE Toggle quick search field Search Home Careers Benefits & Perks Work/Life Balance About Starkville Applicant Notices Campus Security Home Careers at MSU Lead. Discover. Ignite. Explore what makes MSSTATE exceptional. We are positive you’ll find your place at Mississippi State in an atmosphere that welcomes all, cultivates academic excellence, and celebrates service to local communities and throughout the world. Explore Careers Benefits, Balance, and Starkville Benefits & Perks Mississippi State values every employee. That’s why we work hard to give you and your family a benefits package and perks that will keep you thriving, happy, and healthy. Learn More about Benefits and Perks Work/Life balance Managing both your career and your life outside of your career can be challenging. Mississippi State has resources in place to help you succeed in your career and your relationships. Learn More Learn more about work/life balance Making Starkville Home Fall in love with Starkville, “Mississippi’s College Town”. From great eats to local boutiques; astounding nature and abounding culture, Starkville offers a blend of Southern hospitality that will make you proud to call Starkville home. Learn More Learn More about making Starkville home Benefits and Perks Retirement Plans Mississippi State offers both a defined benefit and a defined contribution plan, (optional retirement plan*). We also offer a supplemental retirement plan through the Mississippi Deferred Compensation Plan and Trust 457 for all benefits eligible employees. Learn more about our retirement, including employee contributions and employer matching. * Only certain positions qualify for the optional retirement plan. Visit Retirement Visit Retirement Insurance You are covered from Day 1. Whether you are searching for health, life, dental, vision, disability, cancer, critical care, long term care, or pre-tax flexible spending account plans, we’ve got you covered. Learn more about the various insurance plans and rates. Visit Insurance Insurance Educational Assistance Mississippi State University offers tuition remission benefits to all benefits eligible employees and eligible retirees and their dependents. Benefits eligible employees can take up to six hours per semester, upon approval from their supervisor. Learn more detailed information regarding this benefit. Visit Educational Assistance Time Off VACATION/PERSONAL LEAVE 18 days/per year (144 hours) from the first month until 3 years of service. SICK LEAVE Nine Month faculty earn major medical leave in lieu of personal leave. (15 days/year.) 12-month Faculty and Staff earn 12 days/year from the first month until 3 years of service. HOLIDAYS University employees are afforded 15 paid holidays. Check out all our holidays . Visit Time Off Visit Time Off Other Perks DISCOUNTED ATHLETIC TICKETS For many MSU employees, Bulldog sports are an important part of campus life. MSU employees can purchase discounted season tickets – 20 percent off baseball, men's and women's basketball, and football tickets. Visit Ticket Office Visit Ticket Office MSU GOLF COURSE Regularly ranked as one of the nation's best golf courses, the 6,927 yard MSU Golf Course is an 18 hole, par 72, PGA sanctioned, championship course. MSU employees receive discounts on green fees and semester golf passes. Visit Golf Visit Golf Recognition as a Great Employer MSU is the only Southeastern Conference school to make the 2024 Top 50 list of “America’s Best Large Employers” recently published by Forbes. MSU Forbes Ranking For the ninth consecutive year, Mississippi State University is being honored as an exemplary employer by the Great Colleges to Work For recognition program. Great College to Work For Work/Life Balance The Mississippi State University Work Life Balance Committee aims to act as liaisons and advocates for faculty, staff and administration looking to balance work and life issues by offering support, information, resources and affecting new policies. Several particular topics fall under the scope of this committee, which include but are not limited to dependents, mental and physical health, and workplace policies and procedures. Visit Work/Life Balance Visit Work/Life Balance Fall in Love with Starkville With its small town charm, great food and a thriving main street, Starkville lets you enjoy Southern hospitality while being within hours to Atlanta, Memphis, Nashville, and New Orleans Area Events Come Eat & Shop With Us Cotton District Arts Festival Starkville Community Market Things To Do Find MSU Jobs on Facebook Find MSU Jobs on Instagram Find MSU Jobs on Pinterest Find MSU Jobs on X Twitter Find MSU Jobs on Youtube Mississippi State University Mississippi State, MS 39762 Call (662) 325-2323 (662) 325-2323"
    },
