      "description": "Instructional Designer - Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Learn More about MSU Home Benefits & Perks Work/Life Balance About Starkville Applicant Notices Campus Security My Profile Applicant Login Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Instructional Designer 511193 Main Campus - Starkville, MS Mississippi - Main Campus 042000 - Division of Business Research Professional Regular Full-Time 12-month Opening on: Sep 3 2026 Add to favorites View favorites Position Function: The Instructional Designer works within the College of Business in support of the Boots to Business Revenue Readiness (B2B RR) cooperative agreement funded by the US Small Business Administration (SBA). The follow-on training program known as Boots to Business - Execute and Grow, provides self-paced, on demand, entrepreneurship training to veterans and military spouses nationally. Courses focus on Business Execution and Growth. Serving under the Director of B2B RR, this position assesses training needs, develops and implements self-paced and online training modules in key areas related to entrepreneurship and small business ownership. The follow-on training highlights the shift from ideas/revenue readiness to real-world execution and sustainable growth and provides a deeper five into some specific areas such as financial literacy, financial management, marketing, and cybersecurity basics. Salary Grade :  15 Please see Staff Compensation Structure or Skilled Crafts and Service Maintenance Compensation Schedule for salary ranges.  For salary grade UC, these positions are \"Unclassified\" and salary ranges are determined by the hiring department. Department Profile: Provide online training to veterans, service disable veterans, reservists, national-guard members and transitioning service members interested in starting a business. Essential Duties and Responsibilities: * Design, develop, and deliver self-paced, on-demand, engaging training programs and other learning opportunities focused on entrepreneurship and small business ownership. * Collaborate with B2B RR Director and the SBA Office of Veterans Business Development (OVBD) to identify and get approval for course subjects to be included. * Coordinate with MSU Extension Service for registration platform and self-paced, on-demand delivery using the Canvas platform. * Work with existing training materials to transition to self-paced versions, and/or with subject matter experts to develop new material. * Monitor and report completion and other metrics of effectiveness for training programs. * Coordinate marketing of the courses with the Director and the B2B Program Coordinator. * Utilize good design practices and technologies to facilitate distance instruction. * Assist with the website as needed. * Perform additional duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor's Degree in Instructional Design, Educational Technology, or a Business (Finance or Accounting) degree. 2 years experience demonstrating experience designing and developing online or hybrid courses. Proficiency with Canvas and other learning management systems and related instructional technologies. Proficiency with presentation and/or video editing software (e.g. Preferred Qualifications: Veteran or Military Spouse Master's Degree in instructional design, educational technology, Business (Finance or Accounting) or a related field Knowledge or experience in Small Business Ownership Strong, demonstrated in-person presentation and communication skills Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: * Strong, analytical, problem-solving, research and writing skills. * Strong interpersonal communication skills and the ability to work effectively across organizational levels and with different units and divisions of the university. * Ability to manage multiple tasks, prioritize effectively, and work independently while collaborating with others. Working Conditions and Physical Effort * No unusual physical requirements. Requires no heavy lifting and nearly all work is performed in a comfortable indoor facility. * Travel is normally limited. * Frequent externally imposed deadlines, set and revised beyond one's control. Interruptions influence priorities. Difficult to anticipate nature or volume of work with certainty beyond a few days. Instructions for Applying: Link to apply: http://explore.msujobs.msstate.edu/ All applicants must apply online at www.msujobs.msstate.edu and attach a cover letter, current resume, or curriculum vitae and the complete information for at lease three professional references. Restricted Clause: Position is contingent upon continued availability of funding. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: Mississippi State University is an equal opportunity institution. Discrimination is prohibited in university employment, programs or activities based on race, color, ethnicity, sex, pregnancy, religion, national origin, disability, age, sexual orientation, genetic information, status as a U.S. veteran, or any other status to the extent protected by applicable law. Questions about equal opportunity programs or compliance should be directed to the Office of Civil Rights Compliance, 231 Famous Maroon Band Street, P.O. 6044, Mississippi State, MS 39762, (662) 325-5839. What do I do if I need an accommodation? In compliance with the ADA Amendments Act (ADA), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply for a position with Mississippi State University, please contact the Department of Human Resources Management at tel: (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . If you have any questions regarding this policy, contact the Department of Human Resources Management at (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . Upon request, sections of this job listing are available in large print, and readers are available to assist the visually impaired. Recommended Jobs Assistant/Associate Director of the Center for Entrepreneurship & Outreach Main Campus - Starkville