    "https://explore.msujobs.msstate.edu/jobs/research-associate-i-l-p-s-main-campus-starkville-ms-mississippi-united-states-627ced39-fdd8-47fa-8808-50d41347811f": {
      "title": "Research Associate I (L,P,S)",
      "description": "Research Associate I (L,P,S) - Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Learn More about MSU Home Benefits & Perks Work/Life Balance About Starkville Applicant Notices Campus Security My Profile Applicant Login Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Research Associate I (L,P,S) 511223 Main Campus - Starkville, MS Mississippi - Main Campus 030600 - Stennis Inst of Govt and Comm Dev Professional Regular Full-Time 12-month Opening on: Sep 3 2026 Add to favorites View favorites Position Function: Under general supervision, assists with the planning, coordination, implementation, and evaluation of applied research, planning, data analytics, program evaluation, technical assistance, and grant-funded projects. The incumbent conducts research and analysis, develops reports and project deliverables, supports stakeholder engagement efforts, and contributes to the successful implementation of projects that advance the mission of the John C. Stennis Institute of Government and Community Development. The position reports directly to the Executive Director and works collaboratively with Institute staff, university personnel, government agencies, nonprofit organizations, and community partners throughout Mississippi and the Southeast. Salary Grade :  13 Please see Staff Compensation Structure or Skilled Crafts and Service Maintenance Compensation Schedule for salary ranges.  For salary grade UC, these positions are \"Unclassified\" and salary ranges are determined by the hiring department. Department Profile: The John C. Stennis Institute of Government and Community Development is a public service, training, technical assistance, and applied research unit of Mississippi State University. The Institute works to strengthen the capacity of local governments, nonprofit organizations, community leaders, and public agencies through research, leadership development, strategic planning, policy analysis, civic engagement, community development, and organizational capacity-building initiatives. The Institute serves communities throughout Mississippi and collaborates with federal, state, regional, and local partners to address complex public challenges and improve quality of life. Area of Specialization: Applied Social Science Research, Public Policy, Community Development, Planning, Data Analytics, Program Evaluation, and Grant-funded Project Support Essential Duties and Responsibilities: 1. Assist in the design, coordination, implementation, and evaluation of applied research projects. 2. Collect, manage, analyze, and interpret quantitative and qualitative data using established research methodologies. 3. Conduct literature reviews, policy analyses, environmental scans, needs assessments, and best-practice research. 4. Develop technical reports, white papers, briefing materials, presentations, grant reports, dashboards, and other project deliverables. 5. Support strategic planning initiatives, community assessments, organizational assessments, and program evaluation activities. 6. Assist with implementation and administration of grant-funded projects, including documentation, performance measurement, monitoring activities, and reporting requirements. 7. Maintain project records, databases, data systems, and supporting documentation. 8. Collaborate with Institute staff, university personnel, governmental entities, nonprofit organizations, consultants, and community stakeholders. 9. Assist with proposal development activities, grant applications, and identification of funding opportunities. 10. Prepare and present research findings and project outcomes to governmental, academic, professional, and community audiences. 11. Maintain current knowledge of research methodologies, public policy issues, community development practices, and analytical tools relevant to assigned projects. 12. Travel as necessary to support project implementation, client engagement, field-based activities, and outreach efforts. 13. Perform related duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor's degree in Public Administration, Political Science, Public Policy, Community Development, Urban and Regional Planning, Sociology, Economics, Geography, Data Analytics, or a related field. Rank and salary will be commensurate with the education and/or experience of the candidate. Preferred Qualifications: Master's degree in Public Administration, Public Policy, Community Development, Planning, Political Science, Sociology, Economics, Geography, Data Analytics, or a related field. Experience in one or more of the following areas: • Applied research • Community development • Local government • Public policy analysis • Strategic planning • Program evaluation • Disaster recovery • Organizational capacity building • Grant-funded project administration Demonstrated knowledge of research methods, data collection, analytical techniques, program evaluation, or related areas acquired through academic coursework, research experience, internships, assistantships, or professional employment. Experience with statistical analysis, GIS applications, survey research, data visualization tools, or related analytical software is preferred. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: • Knowledge of social science research methods and analytical approaches. • Ability to collect, organize, analyze, and interpret data from multiple sources. • Strong written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills. • Ability to prepare professional reports, presentations, and technical documents. • Strong organizational, project management, and problem-solving abilities. • Ability to work independently and as part of an interdisciplinary team. • Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with stakeholder groups. • Proficiency in Microsoft Office applications, including Word, Excel, PowerPoint, Teams, and related software. Working Conditions and Physical Effort Work is generally performed in an office environment with regular use of computer equipment. Some travel throughout Mississippi and occasional overnight travel may be required. Occasional evening meetings and participation in project-related events, workshops, conferences, and community engagement activities may be necessary. A valid driver's license and the ability to travel independently may be required. Instructions for Applying: Link to apply: http://explore.msujobs.msstate.edu/ All applicants must apply online and submit a completed application, résumé, cover letter, and any additional materials requested through the Mississippi State University employment system. Restricted Clause: Position is contingent upon continued availability of funding. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: Mississippi State University is an equal opportunity institution. Discrimination is prohibited in university employment, programs or activities based on race, color, ethnicity, sex, pregnancy, religion, national origin, disability, age, sexual orientation, genetic information, status as a U.S. veteran, or any other status to the extent protected by applicable law. Questions about equal opportunity programs or compliance should be directed to the Office of Civil Rights Compliance, 231 Famous Maroon Band Street, P.O. 6044, Mississippi State, MS 39762, (662) 325-5839. What do I do if I need an accommodation? In compliance with the ADA Amendments Act (ADA), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply for a position with Mississippi State University, please contact the Department of Human Resources Management at tel: (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . If you have any questions regarding this policy, contact the Department of Human Resources Management at (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . Upon request, sections of this job listing are available in large print, and readers are available to assist the visually impaired. Recommended Jobs Assistant/Associate Director of the Center for Entrepreneurship & Outreach Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi The Assistant/Associate Director of the Center for Entrepreneurship & Outreach provides strategic leadership and operational oversight for the university’s venture development initiatives. This position is responsible for expanding Mississippi State University’s entrepreneurial ecosystem by supporting technology-based startups, growing Bulldog Innovation Labs, managing CoWork at The Hub, co-leading the VentureCatalyst accelerator, and building strong partnerships across the university.\nThe Associate Director serves as a key liaison between faculty, students, researchers, industry partners, and the Office of Technology Management to increase startup outcomes, startup formation, and entrepreneurial engagement across all colleges. This position will play key role in the expansion of the E-Center offerings, including: investment fund, new accelerator programs, and programs that are run jointly with other colleges and departments. This new position will be expected to teach one of two courses per year. \nKey Performance Indicators\n•\tGrowth in technology-based startups supported through VentureCatalyst.\n•\tIncrease in faculty and student participation in entrepreneurship programs.\n•\tExpansion and utilization of Bulldog Innovation Labs and CoWork at The Hub.\n•\tIncreased collaboration with academic colleges and interdisciplinary programs.\n•\tGrowth in technology spinout companies’ Successful execution of entrepreneurship events, accelerators, and educational programming.\n•\tIncreased external partnerships, mentors, investors, and ecosystem engagement.\n•\tGrant writing and submission Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor Meridian Campus - Meridian, MS, Mississippi. Riley Campus - Meridian, MS, Mississippi. Riley Center - Meridian, MS, Mississippi The Mississippi State University Meridian Campus is seeking an Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor for the Department of Healthcare Administration.  This is a 9-month, tenure track faculty position. Instructional Designer Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi The Instructional Designer works within the College of Business in support of the Boots to Business Revenue Readiness (B2B RR) cooperative agreement funded by the US Small Business Administration (SBA).  The follow-on training program known as Boots to Business - Execute and Grow, provides self-paced, on demand, entrepreneurship training to veterans and military spouses nationally.  Courses focus on Business Execution and Growth.  Serving under the Director of B2B RR, this position assesses training needs, develops and implements self-paced and online training modules in key areas related to entrepreneurship and small business ownership.   The follow-on training highlights the shift from ideas/revenue readiness to real-world execution and sustainable growth and provides a deeper five into some specific areas such as financial literacy, financial management, marketing, and cybersecurity basics. Mississippi State, MS 39762 Phone: (662)325-2323 Facebook Instagram X Youtube Pinterest Cookie Preferences Customer Service at MSState | EEO Statement at MSState | Ethics Line at MSState | Legal Notices at MSState | Annual Security & Fire Report at MSState Mississippi State University is an equal opportunity institution. Discrimination is prohibited in university employment, programs or activities based on race, color, ethnicity, sex, pregnancy, religion, national origin, disability, age, sexual orientation, genetic information, status as a U.S. veteran, or any other status to the extent protected by applicable law. Questions about equal opportunity programs or compliance should be directed to the Office of Civil Rights Compliance , 231 Famous Maroon Band Street, P.O. 6044, Mississippi State, MS 39762 Copyright © 2026 Mississippi State University. All Rights Reserved. Technical problems, contact the Service Desk . Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and it