    "https://explore.msujobs.msstate.edu/jobs/program-assistant-various-locations-in-mississippi-mississippi-united-states-8869cd10-9320-4272-928c-b6ef8ea08738": {
      "title": "Program Assistant",
      "description": "Program Assistant - Various locations in Mississippi, Mississippi, United States Learn More about MSU Home Benefits & Perks Work/Life Balance About Starkville Applicant Notices Campus Security My Profile Applicant Login Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Program Assistant 511208 Various locations in Mississippi Mississippi - Not located on main campus 050405 - CEP-Migrant Ed Support Staff Regular Full-Time 12-month Opening on: Sep 3 2026 Add to favorites View favorites Position Function: The Mississippi Migrant Education Program is a federally funded program geared towards providing migrant students with supplemental education to bridge learning gaps due to the migratory lifestyle. Applicants should be highly self-motivated to provide education services to underserved students in rural areas across the state of Mississippi. The function of the Program Assistant is to support the Migrant Education Program (MEP) through advocacy, outreach, family engagement, and recruitment assistance activities. This position assists migrant children, youth, and families in accessing educational and community resources while promoting awareness of services available through the Migrant Education Program. The Program Assistant assists with identification of potential migrant families and serves as a liaison between migrant families, schools, community organizations, and program staff to help address barriers to educational success. Employees hired into Intermittent positions are limited to working no more than 720 hours per fiscal year. Salary Grade :  9 Please see Staff Compensation Structure or Skilled Crafts and Service Maintenance Compensation Schedule for salary ranges.  For salary grade UC, these positions are \"Unclassified\" and salary ranges are determined by the hiring department. Department Profile: As a land-grant university, MSU is proud to house the Mississippi Migrant Education Service Center which serves agricultural families throughout the state. The Mississippi Migrant Education Service Center is a federal program that offers supplemental and supportive educational services to ensure that migrant children have access to all opportunities that a public education offers. The Mississippi Migrant Education Service Center is funded through the Mississippi Department of Education and is housed at Mississippi State University. Area of Specialization: CEP-Migrant Essential Duties and Responsibilities: Assist with outreach efforts to identify and connect migrant children, youth, and families with available educational services and resources. · Attend state or local and on-going training and meetings including professional development and recruitment support to fulfill the Title I, Part C Migrant Education Program responsibilities. · Support recruitment activities by helping locate prospective migrant families and referring potential participants to program recruiters for eligibility determination. · Establish and maintain positive relationships with migrant families, school personnel, community agencies, agricultural employers, and other stakeholders. · Serve as a liaison between migrant families and schools to facilitate communication and encourage student and family engagement. · Fully understand and establish proper eligibility determinations based on the guidelines outlined in the recruiter’s manual, the Non-Regulatory Guidance, and the statutes governing the MEP. · Follow proper procedures and protocol regarding all identification and recruitment activities. · Provide advocacy and support services to migrant students and families by identifying needs and connecting them with appropriate educational, health, and community resources. · Assist families with understanding school procedures, available services, and educational opportunities. · Participate in community events, school activities, and outreach initiatives designed to increase awareness of the Migrant Education Program. · Maintain records of outreach, advocacy, and family engagement activities as required by program guidelines. · Collaborate with program staff to support student success initiatives and special projects. · Assist with parent engagement activities, workshops, and meetings, including support for Parent Advisory Council activities when appropriate. · Travel extensively (may include weekends) throughout assigned service areas to conduct outreach and provide services to migrant families. · Perform other duties as assigned in support of program goals and objectives. Minimum Qualifications: 1. High school diploma or equivalent. 2. Bilingual (English/Spanish) proficiency 3. Valid driver's license and reliable transportation. 4. Ability to communicate effectively with students, families, school personnel, and community partners. Preferred Qualifications: 1. Experience working with children, youth, families, or community-based programs. 2. Experience working with migrant, multilingual, or underserved populations. 3. Knowledge of community resources and support services available to families. 4. Strong interpersonal, organizational, and communication skills. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Speaks Spanish fluently. Knowledge of state agencies and community services organizations that serve migratory families. Ability to travel extensively. Working Conditions and Physical Effort This position requires travel throughout assigned service areas, including visits to schools, community agencies, homes, and agricultural work sites. Evening and weekend work may be required to accommodate family schedules and community events. Instructions for Applying: Link to apply: http://explore.msujobs.msstate.edu/ Complete the online application and include resume, a cover letter, and minimum of 3 references. Restricted Clause: Position is contingent upon continued availability of funding. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: Mississippi State University is an equal opportunity institution. Discrimination is prohibited in university employment, programs or activities based on race, color, ethnicity, sex, pregnancy, religion, national origin, disability, age, sexual orientation, genetic information, status as a U.S. veteran, or any other status to the extent protected by applicable law. Questions about equal opportunity programs or compliance should be directed to the Office of Civil Rights Compliance, 231 Famous Maroon Band Street, P.O. 6044, Mississippi State, MS 39762, (662) 325-5839. What do I do if I need an accommodation? In compliance with the ADA Amendments Act (ADA), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply for a position with Mississippi State University, please contact the Department of Human Resources Management at tel: (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . If you have any questions regarding this policy, contact the Department of Human Resources Management at (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . Upon request, sections of this job listing are available in large print, and readers are available to assist the visually impaired. Recommended Jobs Assistant/Associate Director of the Center for Entrepreneurship & Outreach Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi The Assistant/Associate Director of the Center for Entrepreneurship & Outreach provides strategic leadership and operational oversight for the university’s venture development initiatives. This position is responsible for expanding Mississippi State University’s entrepreneurial ecosystem by supporting technology-based startups, growing Bulldog Innovation Labs, managing CoWork at The Hub, co-leading the VentureCatalyst accelerator, and building strong partnerships across the university.\nThe Associate Director serves as a key liaison between faculty, students, researchers, industry partners, and the Office of Technology Management to increase startup outcomes, startup formation, and entrepreneurial engagement across all colleges. This position will play key role in the expansion of the E-Center offerings, including: investment fund, new accelerator programs, and programs that are run jointly with other colleges and departments. This new position will be expected to teach one of two courses per year. \nKey Performance Indicators\n•\tGrowth in technology-based startups supported through VentureCatalyst.\n•\tIncrease in faculty and student participation in entrepreneurship programs.\n•\tExpansion and utilization of Bulldog Innovation Labs and CoWork at The Hub.\n•\tIncreased collaboration with academic colleges and interdisciplinary programs.\n•\tGrowth in technology spinout companies’ Successful execution of entrepreneurship events, accelerators, and educational programming.\n•\tIncreased external partnerships, mentors, investors, and ecosystem engagement.\n•\tGrant writing and submission Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor Meridian Campus - Meridian, MS, Mississippi. Riley Campus - Meridian, MS, Mississippi. Riley Center - Meridian, MS, Mississippi The Mississippi State University Meridian Campus is seeking an Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor for the Department of Healthcare Administration.  This is a 9-month, tenure track faculty position. Instructional Designer Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi The Instructional Designer works within the College of Business in support of the Boots to Business Revenue Readiness (B2B RR) cooperative agreement funded by the US Small Business Administration (SBA).  The follow-on training program known as Boots to Business - Execute and Grow, provides self-paced, on demand, entrepreneurship training to veterans and military spouses nationally.  Courses focus on Business Execution and Growth.  Serving under the Director of B2B RR, this position assesses training needs, develops and implements self-paced and online training modules in key areas related to entrepreneurship and small business ownership.   The follow-on training highlights the shift from ideas/revenue readiness to real-world execution and sustainable growth and provides a deeper five into some specific areas such as financial literacy, financial management, marketing, and cybersecurity basics. Mississippi State, MS 39762 Phone: (662)325-2323 Facebook Instagram X Youtube Pinterest Cookie Preferences Customer Service at MSState | EEO Statement at MSState | Ethics Line at MSState | Legal Notices at MSState | Annual Security & Fire Report at MSState Mississippi State University is an equal opportunity institution. Discrimination is prohibited in university employment, programs or activities based on race, color, ethnicity, sex, pregnancy, religion, national origin, disability, age, sexual orientation, genetic information, status as a U.S. veteran, or any other status to the extent protected by applicable law. Questions about equal opportunity programs or compliance should be directed to the Office of Civil Rights Compliance , 231 Famous Maroon Band Street, P.O. 6044, Mississippi State, MS 39762 Copyright © 2026 Mississippi State University. All Rights Reserved. Technical problems, contact the Service Desk . Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all"
