e, or Full Professor for the Department of Healthcare Administration.  This is a 9-month, tenure track faculty position. Instructional Designer Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi The Instructional Designer works within the College of Business in support of the Boots to Business Revenue Readiness (B2B RR) cooperative agreement funded by the US Small Business Administration (SBA).  The follow-on training program known as Boots to Business - Execute and Grow, provides self-paced, on demand, entrepreneurship training to veterans and military spouses nationally.  Courses focus on Business Execution and Growth.  Serving under the Director of B2B RR, this position assesses training needs, develops and implements self-paced and online training modules in key areas related to entrepreneurship and small business ownership.   The follow-on training highlights the shift from ideas/revenue readiness to real-world execution and sustainable growth and provides a deeper five into some specific areas such as financial literacy, financial management, marketing, and cybersecurity basics. Sign Up for Job Alerts Job Alert 0f25036a Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Head Start Positions Support Staff Head Start Positions Support Staff Employment Type Regular Full-Time 12-month Regular Full-Time 12-month Locations Hancock County, Mississippi, United States Hancock County, Mississippi, United States First Name (required) 9b3dc016 Last Name (required) 5a0f3500 Email (required) 06abeefb Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Mississippi State, MS 39762 Phone: (662)325-2323 Facebook Instagram X Youtube Pinterest Cookie Preferences Customer Service at MSState | EEO Statement at MSState | Ethics Line at MSState | Legal Notices at MSState | Annual Security & Fire Report at MSSta