eased collaboration with academic colleges and interdisciplinary programs.\n•\tGrowth in technology spinout companies’ Successful execution of entrepreneurship events, accelerators, and educational programming.\n•\tIncreased external partnerships, mentors, investors, and ecosystem engagement.\n•\tGrant writing and submission Read more Counselor, B2B RR Program 511195 Main Campus - Starkville, MS Mississippi - Main Campus 042000 - Division of Business Research Professional Part-Time 12-Month Research - RES Provide one-on-one counseling and advice to veterans, service-disabled veteran entrepreneurs, Reservists, National Guard members and transitioning service members interested in starting or expanding a small business.  This incumbent will be required to drive and travel to conduct and present the activities of the Veterans Business Outreach Center (VBOC).  Work includes preparing reports and forms, and securing session locations. Read more Counselor, B2B RR Program 511194 Main Campus - Starkville, MS Mississippi - Main Campus 042000 - Division of Business Research Professional Regular Full-Time 12-month Research - RES Provide one-on-one counseling and advice to veterans, service-disabled veteran entrepreneurs, Reservists, National Guard members and transitioning service members interested in starting or expanding a small business.  This incumbent will be required to drive and travel to conduct and present the activities of the Veterans Business Outreach Center (VBOC).  Work includes preparing reports and forms, and securing session locations. Read more Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor 511218 Meridian Campus - Meridian, MS Riley Campus - Meridian, MS Riley Center - Meridian, MS Mississippi - Meridian Campus 313203 - Meridian Healthcare Administration Faculty Regular Full-Time 9-month Academic Affairs-Meridian Campus - AMC The Mississippi State University Meridian Campus is seeking an Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor for the Department of Healthcare Administration.  This is a 9-month, tenure track faculty position. Read more Instructional Designer 511193 Main Campus - Starkville, MS Mississippi - Main Campus 042000 - Division of Business Research Professional Regular Full-Time 12-month Research - RES The Instructional Designer works within the College of Business in support of the Boots to Business Revenue Readiness (B2B RR) cooperative agreement funded by the US Small Business Administration (SBA).  The follow-on training program known as Boots to Business - Execute and Grow, provides self-paced, on demand, entrepreneurship training to veterans and military spouses nationally.  Courses focus on Business Execution and Growth.  Serving under the Director of B2B RR, this position assesses training needs, develops and implements self-paced and online training modules in key areas related to entrepreneurship and small business ownership.   The follow-on training highlights the shift from ideas/revenue readiness to real-world execution and sustainable growth and provides a deeper five into some specific areas such as financial literacy, financial management, marketing, and cybersecurity basics. Read more Communications Supervisor 511226 Main Campus - Starkville, MS Mississippi - Main Campus 470900 - Police Support Staff Regular Full-Time 12-month Student Affairs - STA The Communications Supervisor is responsible for the communications center at the Mississippi State University (MSU) Police Department, including coordinating operations, providing supervision and guidance to communication officers, serving as the field training officer, managing multiple transmitting and receiving devices, communicating with both internal and external sources, and assisting the Dispatchers in the direction of operational message traffic within the unit, and reports to the Support Division Lieutenant. Read more Research Associate I (L,P,S) 511223 Main Campus - Starkville, MS Mississippi - Main Campus 030600 - Stennis Inst of Govt and Comm Dev Professional Regular Full-Time 12-month Research - RES Under general supervision, assists with the planning, coordination, implementation, and evaluation of applied research, planning, data analytics, program evaluation, technical assistance, and grant-funded projects. The incumbent conducts research and analysis, develops reports and project deliverables, supports stakeholder engagement efforts, and contributes to the successful implementation of projects that advance the mission of the John C. Stennis Institute of Government and Community Development.\n\nThe position reports directly to the Executive Director and works collaboratively with Institute staff, university personnel, government agencies, nonprofit organizations, and community partners throughout Mississippi and the Southeast. Read more Program Assistant 511208 Various locations in Mississippi Mississippi - Not located on main campus 050405 - CEP-Migrant Ed Support Staff Regular Full-Time 12-month Research - RES The Mississippi Migrant Education Program is a federally funded program geared towards providing migrant students with supplemental education to bridge learning gaps due to the migratory lifestyle. Applicants should be highly self-motivated to provide education services to underserved students in rural areas across the state of Mississippi.\n\nThe function of the Program Assistant is to support the Migrant Education Program (MEP) through advocacy, outreach, family engagement, and recruitment assistance activities. This position assists migrant children, youth, and families in accessing educational and community resources while promoting awareness of services available through the Migrant Education Program. The Program Assistant assists with identification of potential migrant families and serves as a liaison between migrant families, schools, community organizations, and program staff to help address barriers to educational success. Read more Head Start Monitoring Coordinator 511199 MS Gulf C