 resources, handbooks, policies, and procedures necessary to establish a new DPT program, aligned with the university's mission, vision, and CAPTE standards. As a founding member of the faculty team, there is also a responsibility for developing community relationships and clinical contracts. The overarching goal is to establish processes that ensure that the clinical education component of the curriculum meets accreditation standards and is intentionally integrated within the curriculum. As the program grows, there will be a continued need to develop new sites and to assess relationships and outcomes related to clinical education performance, student development, and program outcomes. \n\nThe DCE is responsible for planning, developing, coordinating, monitoring, and assessing the clinical education component of the program. The DCE collaborates with and mentors students through the clinical education experience. Additional responsibilities include planning and implementing educational opportunities for clinical educators; assisting with recruitment and admissions processes; advising students; providing service to the department, college, and community as strategically planned and appointed; participating in scholarly endeavors; and other duties as assigned by the PT Department Head/Program Director. Read more Intermittent Worker 511184 Meridian Campus - Meridian, MS Riley Campus - Meridian, MS Riley Center - Meridian, MS Mississippi - Meridian Campus 313218 - Meridian - School of Nursing Intermittent Worker Intermittent Academic Affairs-Meridian Campus - AMC The School of Nursing seeks to hire intermittent workers to support program operations on an as-needed basis and to serve in a variety of roles depending on program needs. Read more Communications Specialist 510981 Main Campus - Starkville, MS Mississippi - Main Campus 053700 - NRTC-Nat'l Research Ctr Blindness Professional Regular Full-Time 12-month Research - RES Looking for a communication role where your work truly matters? Join the National Research & Training Center on Blindness & Low Vision (NRTC) at Mississippi State University as a Communications Specialist and help promote innovative research, training, and products that support people who are blind or have low vision across the country. The position's primary purpose is to coordinate NRTC communications and marketing efforts, including promoting center activities, research results, products, training, and technical assistance opportunities to a national audience. Read more Extension Program Associate 511192 Jones County Mississippi - Not located on main campus 019434 - MSU Extension- Jones County Support Staff Regular Full-Time 12-month Agri. Forestry and Vet Medicine - MSUES - GEX The Extension Program Associate assists the Regional Extension Coordinator in the development and implementation of county Extension programs and is administratively responsible to the Regional Extension Coordinator. Read more Web Developer 511189 Main Campus - Starkville, MS Mississippi - Main Campus 011400 - Extension Center for Tech Outreach Professional Regular Full-Time 12-month Agri. Forestry and Vet Medicine - MSUES - GEX Provides web development for select Extension Service websites, consisting primarily of a comprehensive range of websites built in content management systems such as Drupal and WordPress, and various other web applications. Read more Director of Student Services, Meridian - Internal Recruitment Only 511164 Meridian Campus - Meridian, MS Riley Campus - Meridian, MS Riley Center - Meridian, MS Mississippi - Meridian Campus 313213 - Sonny Montgomery Advise/Career Ctr Professional Regular Full-Time 12-month Academic Affairs-Meridian Campus - AMC The Director of Student Services is responsible for leading, developing, and managing programs, services, and resources that promote student success. Read more Research Associate I or II 511197 Main Campus - Starkville, MS Mississippi - Main Campus 191000 - Geosystems Research Institute Professional Regular Full-Time 12-month Research - RES The Geosystems Research Institute (GRI) at Mississippi State University (MSU) is seeking a highly motivated and self-driven Research Associate I or II to support a NOAA-funded research project focused on drought assessment, non-stationarity, and regionalization across the southeastern United States.\nThe successful candidate will work as part of an interdisciplinary research team conducting hydrologic, meteorological, statistical, and geospatial analyses. The Research Associate will be involved in all stages of formal project analysis and regionalization efforts, including data acquisition and preparation, drought characterization, time-series analysis, statistical modeling, geospatial analysis, regional classification, interpretation of results, and preparation of research products.\nCandidates may have primary expertise in either quantitative/statistical analysis or geospatial/scientific data analysis. Applicants with experience spanning both areas are particularly encouraged to apply.\nThe position will involve working with large environmental datasets and developing reproducible analytical workflows using Python, R, GIS, and related scientific computing tools. The Research Associate will collaborate closely with project investigators and other team members and will contribute to technical reports, scientific publications, presentations, data products, and other project deliverables Read more Planning and Assessment Coordinator 511205 Main Campus - Starkville, MS Mississippi - Main Campus 441106 - Student Affairs Assessment Office Professional Regular Full-Time 12-month Student Affairs - STA The Planning and Assessment Coordinator is primarily responsible for facilitating programs, services, and activities in support of the Division of Student Affairs’ goals, objectives, and strategies. Working in the Office of Planning and Assessment, activities include, but are not limited to, assisting departments in the development of success strategies, coordinating activities across the division in support of strategic goals and objectives, and working with the Vice President for Student Affairs team in the development and implementation of policies and procedures. Read more Sr. Payroll Assistant 510437 Main Campus - Starkville, MS Mississippi - Main Campus 450200 - Office of the Controller/Treasurer Support Staff Regular Full-Time 12-month Division of Finance and Administration - BSA Performs advanced fiscal and clerical tasks within the University Budget/Payroll Department of the Controller’s Office. Read more *Intermittent Worker 511201 Biloxi, MS Mississippi - Not located on main campus 440900 - Vice President for Research Intermittent Worker Intermittent Research - RES This position will temporarily serve as the Digital Forensics Analyst Technical Lead for the MCI facility at the Mississippi Gulf Coast Community College. Read more Research Engineer II, III or Senior 511121 Madison County Mississippi - Not located on main campus 193602 - CAVS Extension Professional Regular Full-Time 12-month Research - RES As a Research Engineer II, III, or Senior, you will play a crucial role in the support of Mississippi manufacturers and public-sector partners by assisting companies with the assessment, design, implementation, and maintenance of automation systems that improve productivity, quality, and safety. This position plays a key role in advancing economic development and innovation across the state through hands-on engineering support, applied research, and professional development initiatives. Must be a U.S. Citizen or Permanent Resident. Read more Research Engineer I, II, III or Senior 511122 Madison County Mississippi - Not located on main campus 193602 - CAVS Extension Professional Regular Full-Time 12-month Research - RES As a Research Engineer I, II, III, or Senior, you will play a crucial role in the support of Mississippi manufacturers and public-sector partners by assisting companies with the assessment, design, implementation, and maintenance of automation systems that improve productivity, quality, and safety. This position plays a key role in advancing economic development and innovation across the state through hands-on engineering support, applied research, and professional development initiatives. Must be a U.S. Citizen or Permanent Resident. Read more Project Coordinator - Internal Recruitment 511187 Meridian Campus - Meridian, MS Riley Campus - Meridian, MS Riley Center - Meridian, MS Mississippi - Meridian Campus 313223 - School of Health Professions Professional Regular Full-Time 12-month Academic Affairs-Meridian Campus - AMC The Project Coordinator provides administrative, operational, and strategic support for the School of Health Professions. This position is responsible for coordinating projects and initiatives across multiple functional areas, including sponsored projects administration, compliance monitoring, accreditation support, communications, policy management, donor relations, external partnerships, and special events. The Project Coordinator works closely with the Dean, Associate Deans, Department Heads, program directors, faculty, staff, university offices, community partners, and external stakeholders to advance the School's strategic priorities and ensure the efficient execution of key initiatives. Read more Engineering Shop Manager 510943 Main Campus - Starkville, MS Mississippi - Main Campus 010300 - Ag & Bio Engineering Professional Regular Full-Time 12-month Agri. Forestry and Vet Medicine - CALS - AGR The individual filling this position will be responsible for coordination of labor and activities in the ABE Machine Shop, ensuring good organization and safety.  The individual will work with researchers’ conceptual designs and provide practical design and construction.  The individual will oversee other workspaces belonging to ABE.  The individual will also be involved in teaching and overseeing students in the use of shop machines. Read more Extension Agent 511188 Desoto County Mississippi - Not located on main campus 019217 - MSU Extension- Desoto County Extension Agent Professional Regular Full-Time 12-month Agri. Forestry and Vet Medicine - MSUES - GEX Responsible for providing leadership in the development, implementation, and evaluation of a comprehensive non-formal, experiential educational program in the area of positive youth development (4-H). The Extension Agent serves as a member of the county team to determine effective programming priorities and delivery methods for the community. Read more Assistant Professor 511029 Main Campus - Starkville, MS Mississippi - Main Campus 012000 - Biochemistry Nutrition Health Promo Faculty Regular Full-Time 9-month Agri. Forestry and Vet Medicine - CALS - AGR The Department of Biochemistry, Nutrition and Health Promotion (BNHP) at Mississippi State University (MSU) seeks to fill a 9-month tenure-track position to begin January 2027. The successful candidate will hold a 60% appointment in teaching through the College of Agriculture and Life Sciences and a 40% appointment in research through the Mississippi Agricultural and Forestry Experiment Station. The successful candidate will teach both undergraduate and graduate courses in Biochemistry. In addition, the candidate will be expected to develop a nationally recognized research program in their area of expertise that aligns with the department’s mission through publication of peer-reviewed articles, procurement of extramural funding, and mentoring graduate students. The successful candidate will also support Biochemistry’s student recruitment and retention efforts. Read more Assistant or Associate Professor 511092 Main Campus - Starkville, MS Mississippi - Main Campus 011300 - Animal & Dairy Science Faculty Regular Full-Time 12-month Agri. Forestry and Vet Medicine - CALS - AGR The Department of Animal and Dairy Sciences is currently seeking an Assistant or Associate Professor for a 12-month tenure track (20% teaching, 40% research, 40% Extension) position with an emphasis in dairy science. Read more Assistant/Associate/Full Professor 511124 Main Campus - Starkville, MS Mississippi - Main Campus 011100 - Plant and Soil Sciences Faculty Regular Full-Time 12-month Agri. Forestry and Vet Medicine - CALS - AGR The Department of Plant and Soil Sciences in the College of Agriculture and Life Sciences at Mississippi State University is seeking applicants for an Assistant/Associate/Full Professor with a research (70%)/teaching (30%) appointment in corn and small grain agronomics. This position will be a 12-month tenure track appointment with an anticipated start date of January 1, 2027. \n\nFor candidates with experience or appointment at the Associate or Full Professor levels, the position may also include co-appointment as The Triplett Corn Promotion Board Professor. This Professorship carries the professorship title, and additional salary stipend and some programmatic support. The successful candidate will be expected to collaborate with faculty and staff from the Department of Plant and Soil Sciences as well as with other departments across campus and other institutions. Read more Events Coordinator (MSU Riley) 511137 Meridian Campus - Meridian, MS Riley Campus - Meridian, MS Riley Center - Meridian, MS Mississippi - Meridian Campus 313214 - MSU-Riley Center Professional Regular Full-Time 12-month Academic Affairs-Meridian Campus - AMC Responsible for coordinating and/or overseeing preparation of conference facility to accommodate all conference, social and internal events and provide on-site coordination as the client's liaison during meetings and events held in the facility. Read more Coordinator, Academic Advising & Student Engagement 511183 Meridian Campus - Meridian, MS Riley Campus - Meridian, MS Riley Center - Meridian, MS Mississippi - Meridian Campus 313223 - School of Health Professions Professional Regular