am Manager 510760 Main Campus - Starkville, MS Mississippi - Main Campus 061700 - Mechanical Engineering Professional Regular Full-Time 12-month Academic Affairs-College of Engineering - AEN The Department of Mechanical Engineering at Mississippi State University seeks a full-time, twelve-month Program Manager to lead the Mississippi State METAL Hub Mobile STEM Initiative within the Innovation Design and Engineering Educational Laboratory (IDEELab).\n\nThe Program Manager will serve as the operational and programmatic lead for a statewide mobile advanced manufacturing and STEM education platform designed to deliver hands-on workforce development experiences directly to K-12 students, educators, and communities throughout Mississippi. This position will oversee mobile trailer operations, curriculum development, outreach programming, event coordination, stakeholder engagement, and workforce development activities supporting the state's future manufacturing talent pipeline.\n\nThe successful candidate will coordinate school visits, industry engagement activities, educator workshops, summer programs, public outreach events, workforce development demonstrations, and mobile training deployments. The position will work closely with K-12 schools, community colleges, industry partners, workforce organizations, government agencies, and economic development entities to expand awareness of advanced manufacturing careers and educational opportunities.\n\nIn addition to leading the METAL Mobile STEM Initiative, the Program Manager will support IDEELab workforce development, outreach, recruiting, and industry engagement activities that advance the mission of the Mechanical Engineering Department and Bagley College of Engineering. Read more Custodian I Day Shift (4:00am-1:00pm) 510750 Main Campus - Starkville, MS Mississippi - Main Campus 490400 - Custodial Services Support Staff Regular Full-Time 12-month Division of Finance and Administration - BSA To perform duties necessary for